From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: win32u: REG_OPTION_OPEN_LINK is the OBJ_OPENLINK attribute

win32u's reg_create_key() passed REG_OPTION_OPEN_LINK to NtCreateKey as a
create option, which the server ignores; RegCreateKeyEx turns it into the
OBJ_OPENLINK attribute. So when write_source_to_registry() "opened the link"
at Control\Video\{gpu}\NNNN to point it at a display source, it followed the
link instead: the new target was written into the old target's key, and the
link kept naming whichever source first took that index.

With a virtual desktop that is the physical output: the first update, before
the virtual source exists, gives it index 0; afterwards the virtual source is
index 0 and the physical one index 1, but the stale link still sends index 0
to the physical source's key. Both indices then read back the same source, a
monitor is left with no source, win32u reports its 1024x768 default as the
primary screen, and the taskbar is laid out for it, whatever the real screen
size. Whether it bites depends on timing -- on whether the first display
update in a session runs before the virtual desktop exists -- which is why
Stained Glass's session gate passed for a long time and then failed on every
run on the same machine.

Translate the option as RegCreateKeyEx does. Established with a standalone
test: creating an existing link fails (as on Windows), and retargeting works
only through an OBJ_OPENLINK handle.

--- a/dlls/win32u/font.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/font.c
@@ -526,6 +526,13 @@
     attr.Attributes = 0;
     attr.SecurityDescriptor = NULL;
     attr.SecurityQualityOfService = NULL;
+    /* As in RegCreateKeyEx: REG_OPTION_OPEN_LINK is the OBJ_OPENLINK attribute,
+     * not a create option. Passed as an option it was ignored, so "open the
+     * link to retarget it" followed the link instead, wrote the new target
+     * into the old target's key, and the link kept pointing where it did --
+     * display sources then read back another source's settings. */
+    if (options & REG_OPTION_OPEN_LINK) attr.Attributes |= OBJ_OPENLINK;
+    options &= ~REG_OPTION_OPEN_LINK;
 
     status = NtCreateKey( &ret, MAXIMUM_ALLOWED, &attr, 0, NULL, options, disposition );
     if (status == STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_NOT_FOUND)
